{"product_id":"man-in-the-dark","title":"Man in the Dark","description":"\u003cp\u003eMan in the Dark is Paul Auster課ｪs brilliant, devastating novel about the many realities we inhabit as wars flame all around us.Seventy-two-year-old August Brill is recovering from a car accident in his daughter課ｪs house in Vermont. When sleep refuses to come, he lies in bed and tells himself stories, struggling to push back thoughts about things he would prefer to forget課ﾓhis wife課ｪs recent death and the horrific murder of his granddaughter課ｪs boyfriend, Titus. The retired book critic imagines a parallel world in which America is not at war with Iraq but with itself. In this other America the twin towers did not fall and the 2000 election results led to secession, as state after state pulled away from the union and a bloody civil war ensued. As the night progresses, Brill課ｪs story grows increasingly intense, and what he is so desperately trying to avoid insists on being told. Joined in the early hours by his granddaughter, he gradually opens up to her and recounts the story of his marriage. After she falls asleep, he at last finds the courage to revisit the trauma of Titus課ｪs death.Passionate and shocking, Man in the Dark is a novel of our moment, a book that forces us to confront the blackness of night even as it celebrates the existence of ordinary joys in a world capable of the most grotesque violence.*Time Out (Chicago)\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 141 x 223\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Paul Auster\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9780571240760\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Hardcover\u003cbr\u003e\nPages: 192\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookloopbook.com","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45262380794009,"sku":"16RA-4-9780571240760","price":20.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/67e7e729a69e4_Man_20in_20the_20Dark_20Paul_20Auster.jpg?v=1743435937","url":"https:\/\/bookloopbook.com\/products\/man-in-the-dark","provide